# Normalize text to LF in the repository, on every platform.
#
# Without this the Windows CI runner checks out with core.autocrlf=true,
# every Go source lands as CRLF, and `gofmt -l` reports the entire tree as
# unformatted — a platform-dependent false positive that made the gofmt
# gate fail on windows-latest while passing on Linux and macOS. Line
# endings belong to the repository, not to the developer's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch binary payloads: normalizing these would corrupt them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# Patch/report artifacts that must round-trip byte-for-byte.
*.sha256 text eol=lf
*.patch text eol=lf
